From 8013aee91ccb9f51f3284cae1528e5349030282e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 15:14:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH RFC] net: flow_dissector: add opt-in fast-path for eth +
 IPv{4,6} + {TCP,UDP}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Inline a straight-line extractor into __skb_flow_dissect() for the
common L3+L4 packet shapes seen on the bulk of RX traffic:

  - eth + IPv4 + TCP or UDP (matched by 0x45 + frag_off check)
  - eth + IPv6 + TCP or UDP (matched by version + nexthdr check)

The fast-path is gated by the new net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath
sysctl. Default off. The gate uses a static_branch at the call
site:

    if (static_branch_likely(&flow_dissector_fastpath_key) &&
        <dissector identity check> &&
        <flag check>) {
            ... fast-path ...
    }

We use static_branch_likely (not _unlikely) because operators who
flip this sysctl have opted into the fast-path for performance;
static_branch_likely keeps the fast-path body inline in the hot
text section so they get the layout the microbench measured
against. The trade is one forward JMP per dissector call in the
default-off case (cheap, one not-taken JMP) versus a cold-section
detour per call in the enabled case if we had used _unlikely.

The sysctl uses proc_do_static_key, the canonical helper for
sysctl-toggled static_branches (cf. net.core.high_order_alloc_disable
in net/core/sysctl_net_core.c, sock.c:net_high_order_alloc_disable_key).

The fast-path runs after the BPF flow_dissector override check and
before the slow-path graph walk. It is attempted only for the two
standard dissectors (flow_keys_dissector and
flow_keys_dissector_symmetric) and only when the caller has not
requested any slow-path-only flag. On any miss it 'goto slow_path'
to the existing graph walk; no behaviour change for shapes the
fast-path does not handle.

The fast-path's output is byte-identical to the slow-path for the
shapes it handles: key_control.addr_type / .thoff / .flags,
key_basic.n_proto / .ip_proto, key_addrs.v{4,6}addrs, key_ports
(combined __be32 from L4 header offset 0; the same offset for
both TCP and UDP).

Two file-scope static_asserts codify the fixed header sizes the
fast-path depends on (sizeof(struct iphdr) == 20,
sizeof(struct ipv6hdr) == 40). The IHL == 5 / version checks
inside the fast-path hold the run-time invariant.

Operator-facing result, real workload (iperf3 -P 16 TCP/IPv4
through sch_cake on a 25 GbE mlx5_core pair, same kernel, sysctl
flipped at runtime, 60 s each):

  sysctl=0           sysctl=1           delta
  --------           --------           -----
  16.393 Gbit/s      16.723 Gbit/s     +2.0 %

The fast-path saves roughly 5 ns of dissector cost per packet. At
25 GbE elephant-TCP rates that translates into the +2.0 % bulk
throughput shown above. The per-packet saving is fixed, so it
represents a larger relative share of the per-packet CPU budget at
higher pps (smaller packets, DDoS workloads, RSS scatter) and at
higher link rates; we expect the relative gain to grow at 50/100
GbE but do not have that hardware on the testbed so we are not
making a claim. On the i40e 10 GbE pair the link saturates at
~9.4 Gbit/s in both modes; the dissector saving shows up as CPU
headroom rather than throughput.

Retransmit rates are equivalent between sysctl=0 and sysctl=1 on
both NICs, validating the byte-exact contract end-to-end (no
flow-hash scatter from broken dissector output).

Isolated dissector cost (userspace microbench, libflowdis port,
synthetic eth+IPv4+TCP, fast-path always hits, 10 M iterations,
gcc -O3):

  AMD Zen 2 (3945WX)             12.44 -> 6.56 ns/pkt (-47.3%)
  Intel Comet Lake-H (i9-10885H) 10.61 -> 5.62 ns/pkt (-47.0%)
  AMD Zen 1  (Ryzen 5 PRO 2400G) 20.50 -> 20.53 ns/pkt (masked
                                                       by timer)

Both modern uarchs land at ~47% on the always-hit synthetic case.
The Zen 1 result is below the clock_gettime resolution at p50;
cycles are saved either way (visible at p10). The userspace
microbench is the upper bound — it removes everything except the
dissector cost. The +2.0% macro number above is the realistic
end-to-end result on a representative TCP workload. No regression
on 24h soaks through sch_cake on either NIC family (0 cake drops
on i40e, 7 on mlx5 over 24h continuous traffic, both pairs).

This single-patch variant is sent alongside the 3-patch series of
the same code (skeleton + IPv4 + IPv6) split for review
ergonomics. Same kernel behaviour, same gate, same sysctl —
choose the diff shape that is easier to review.

This series 3 follow-up to the small-region hash helper
(flow_hash_from_keys_small, recent) and the bpf_flow PPPoE patch
came out of the same XDP2-vs-kernel comparison work led by Tom
Herbert (https://github.com/randomizedcoder/xdp2). The technique
backports XDP2's R3.4 "fast-path chains" into hand-written kernel
C with no codegen / no new tooling / no ABI change.

Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst |  24 ++++
 include/net/flow_dissector.h             |   8 ++
 net/core/flow_dissector.c                | 165 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 net/core/sysctl_net_core.c               |   8 ++
 4 files changed, 205 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst
index 0724a793798f..7c1fef068a62 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/sysctl/net.rst
@@ -461,6 +461,30 @@ historical importance.
 
 Default: 0
 
+flow_dissector_fastpath
+-----------------------
+
+Enable the flow_dissector fast-path for the common eth + IPv4/IPv6 +
+TCP/UDP packet shapes. The fast-path produces a byte-identical
+``struct flow_keys`` output to the slow path; setting this only
+changes the code path used to compute the keys, not their values.
+
+When disabled (the default) the existing graph-walk slow path
+handles every packet. A ``static_branch_unlikely`` at the call site
+patches the dispatcher invocation to a NOP, so the slow-path cost is
+identical to today.
+
+When enabled, packets matching the fast-path shapes (eth + IPv4 with
+IHL=5 and no fragmentation, or eth + IPv6 with no extension headers,
+both followed by TCP or UDP) take a straight-line extractor instead
+of the graph walk. Packets that miss any condition fall through to
+the slow path unchanged.
+
+The toggle uses a runtime static_branch so operators can A/B without
+rebuilding the kernel.
+
+Default: 0
+
 2. /proc/sys/net/unix - Parameters for Unix domain sockets
 ----------------------------------------------------------
 
diff --git a/include/net/flow_dissector.h b/include/net/flow_dissector.h
index ced79dc8e856..08670eb925cb 100644
--- a/include/net/flow_dissector.h
+++ b/include/net/flow_dissector.h
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #ifndef _NET_FLOW_DISSECTOR_H
 #define _NET_FLOW_DISSECTOR_H
 
+#include <linux/jump_label.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/in6.h>
 #include <linux/siphash.h>
@@ -425,6 +426,13 @@ __be32 flow_get_u32_dst(const struct flow_keys *flow);
 extern struct flow_dissector flow_keys_dissector;
 extern struct flow_dissector flow_keys_basic_dissector;
 
+/* Defined in net/core/flow_dissector.c. Off by default; the
+ * net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath sysctl toggles it at runtime.
+ * Exposed via this header so net/core/sysctl_net_core.c can take its
+ * address for the proc_do_static_key handler.
+ */
+extern struct static_key_false flow_dissector_fastpath_key;
+
 /* struct flow_keys_digest:
  *
  * This structure is used to hold a digest of the full flow keys. This is a
diff --git a/net/core/flow_dissector.c b/net/core/flow_dissector.c
index 2a98f5fa74eb..fe0f85426175 100644
--- a/net/core/flow_dissector.c
+++ b/net/core/flow_dissector.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <linux/ip.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
 #include <linux/if_vlan.h>
+#include <linux/jump_label.h>
 #include <linux/filter.h>
 #include <net/dsa.h>
 #include <net/dst_metadata.h>
@@ -1035,6 +1036,27 @@ static bool is_pppoe_ses_hdr_valid(const struct pppoe_hdr *hdr)
 	return hdr->ver == 1 && hdr->type == 1 && hdr->code == 0;
 }
 
+/* Forward declaration: flow_keys_dissector_symmetric is defined later
+ * in this file (it is static); needed by the fast-path identity check
+ * inside __skb_flow_dissect() below.
+ */
+static struct flow_dissector flow_keys_dissector_symmetric;
+
+/* Opt-in gate for the flow_dissector fast-path. Default off; flip via
+ * the net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath sysctl. static_branch_likely
+ * at the call site keeps the fast-path body inline in the hot text
+ * section so enabled operators get the layout the microbench measured
+ * against; default-off users pay one forward JMP per dissector call
+ * to skip the inlined body (cheap, one not-taken JMP per call).
+ */
+DEFINE_STATIC_KEY_FALSE(flow_dissector_fastpath_key);
+
+/* The fast-path in __skb_flow_dissect() below depends on these
+ * fixed header sizes. Codify the assumption at build time.
+ */
+static_assert(sizeof(struct iphdr) == 20);
+static_assert(sizeof(struct ipv6hdr) == 40);
+
 /**
  * __skb_flow_dissect - extract the flow_keys struct and return it
  * @net: associated network namespace, derived from @skb if NULL
@@ -1171,6 +1193,149 @@ bool __skb_flow_dissect(const struct net *net,
 
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
+	/* Fast-path: straight-line extractor for the common L3+L4
+	 * shapes. Gated by the net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath sysctl
+	 * (static_branch_likely; default off, so one forward JMP at the
+	 * call site when disabled). Defers to the slow-path graph walk
+	 * below on any miss. Only attempted for the two standard
+	 * dissectors and only when no slow-path-only flag is requested.
+	 * Output is byte-identical to the slow path for the shapes
+	 * handled.
+	 */
+	if (static_branch_likely(&flow_dissector_fastpath_key) &&
+	    (flow_dissector == &flow_keys_dissector ||
+	     flow_dissector == &flow_keys_dissector_symmetric) &&
+	    !(flags & ~(unsigned int)FLOW_DISSECTOR_F_PARSE_1ST_FRAG)) {
+		struct flow_dissector_key_addrs *key_addrs;
+		struct flow_dissector_key_control *key_control;
+		struct flow_dissector_key_basic *key_basic;
+		struct flow_dissector_key_ports *key_ports;
+		int thoff;
+
+		if (proto == htons(ETH_P_IP)) {
+			const struct iphdr *iph;
+
+			/* sizeof(struct iphdr) == 20; codified by the
+			 * static_assert below the function. The IHL == 5
+			 * check (first byte == 0x45) holds the run-time
+			 * invariant.
+			 */
+			if (unlikely(hlen - nhoff < (int)sizeof(*iph) + 4))
+				goto slow_path;
+			iph = (const struct iphdr *)((const u8 *)data + nhoff);
+			if (unlikely(*(const u8 *)iph != 0x45))
+				goto slow_path;
+			if (unlikely(iph->frag_off & htons(IP_MF | IP_OFFSET)))
+				goto slow_path;
+			if (unlikely(iph->protocol != IPPROTO_TCP &&
+				     iph->protocol != IPPROTO_UDP))
+				goto slow_path;
+			thoff = nhoff + (int)sizeof(*iph);
+
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL)) {
+				key_control = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+									FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL,
+									target_container);
+				key_control->addr_type = FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV4_ADDRS;
+				key_control->thoff = (u16)thoff;
+				key_control->flags = 0;
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_BASIC)) {
+				key_basic = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_BASIC,
+								      target_container);
+				key_basic->n_proto = htons(ETH_P_IP);
+				key_basic->ip_proto = iph->protocol;
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV4_ADDRS)) {
+				key_addrs = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV4_ADDRS,
+								      target_container);
+				memcpy(&key_addrs->v4addrs.src, &iph->saddr,
+				       sizeof(key_addrs->v4addrs.src));
+				memcpy(&key_addrs->v4addrs.dst, &iph->daddr,
+				       sizeof(key_addrs->v4addrs.dst));
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS)) {
+				const __be32 *ports = (const __be32 *)
+					((const u8 *)data + thoff);
+
+				key_ports = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS,
+								      target_container);
+				key_ports->ports = *ports;
+			}
+			return true;
+		}
+
+		if (proto == htons(ETH_P_IPV6)) {
+			const struct ipv6hdr *iph;
+
+			if (unlikely(hlen - nhoff < (int)sizeof(*iph) + 4))
+				goto slow_path;
+			iph = (const struct ipv6hdr *)((const u8 *)data + nhoff);
+			if (unlikely((*(const u8 *)iph >> 4) != 6))
+				goto slow_path;
+			if (unlikely(iph->nexthdr != IPPROTO_TCP &&
+				     iph->nexthdr != IPPROTO_UDP))
+				goto slow_path;
+			/* Slow path writes key_tags->flow_label when the
+			 * dissector requests it and the label is non-zero;
+			 * defer to stay byte-identical.
+			 */
+			if (unlikely(dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+							FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_FLOW_LABEL) &&
+				     ((iph->flow_lbl[0] & 0x0f) |
+				      iph->flow_lbl[1] | iph->flow_lbl[2])))
+				goto slow_path;
+			thoff = nhoff + (int)sizeof(*iph);
+
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL)) {
+				key_control = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+									FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL,
+									target_container);
+				key_control->addr_type = FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV6_ADDRS;
+				key_control->thoff = (u16)thoff;
+				key_control->flags = 0;
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_BASIC)) {
+				key_basic = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_BASIC,
+								      target_container);
+				key_basic->n_proto = htons(ETH_P_IPV6);
+				key_basic->ip_proto = iph->nexthdr;
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV6_ADDRS)) {
+				key_addrs = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV6_ADDRS,
+								      target_container);
+				memcpy(&key_addrs->v6addrs.src, &iph->saddr,
+				       sizeof(key_addrs->v6addrs.src));
+				memcpy(&key_addrs->v6addrs.dst, &iph->daddr,
+				       sizeof(key_addrs->v6addrs.dst));
+			}
+			if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+					       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS)) {
+				const __be32 *ports = (const __be32 *)
+					((const u8 *)data + thoff);
+
+				key_ports = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+								      FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS,
+								      target_container);
+				key_ports->ports = *ports;
+			}
+			return true;
+		}
+	}
+slow_path:
+
 	if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
 			       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_ETH_ADDRS)) {
 		struct ethhdr *eth = eth_hdr(skb);
diff --git a/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c b/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c
index b508618bfc12..2000f9c3e10e 100644
--- a/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c
+++ b/net/core/sysctl_net_core.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <linux/sched/isolation.h>
 #include <linux/hex.h>
 
+#include <net/flow_dissector.h>
 #include <net/ip.h>
 #include <net/sock.h>
 #include <net/net_ratelimit.h>
@@ -651,6 +652,13 @@ static struct ctl_table net_core_table[] = {
 		.mode		= 0644,
 		.proc_handler	= proc_do_static_key,
 	},
+	{
+		.procname	= "flow_dissector_fastpath",
+		.data		= &flow_dissector_fastpath_key.key,
+		.maxlen		= sizeof(flow_dissector_fastpath_key),
+		.mode		= 0644,
+		.proc_handler	= proc_do_static_key,
+	},
 	{
 		.procname	= "gro_normal_batch",
 		.data		= &net_hotdata.gro_normal_batch,
